  <section class="content-grid">
    <article class="main-card">
      <h2 id="quick-summary">Quick Summary</h2>
      <p>
        Renting a car at Faro International Airport (FAO) is one of the most efficient ways to reach the Algarve’s
        coastline and inland towns. Major agencies maintain desks directly within the Arrivals Hall, allowing travelers
        to complete paperwork and walk to the nearby car collection area without needing a shuttle. At the same time,
        several off-airport providers also serve Faro and usually require a meeting point and short transfer.
      </p>
      <p>
        For travelers heading straight into the Algarve, a rental at Faro Airport often makes immediate practical sense.
        For travelers staying in one walkable town or moving only between major cities, it may be less necessary.
      </p>

      <h2 id="inside-terminal-and-on-airport-rental-options">Inside-Terminal and On-Airport Rental Options</h2>
      <p>
        At Faro International Airport, car rental desks are located within the main terminal building. According to the
        airport’s current rental information, the primary service counters are in the Arrivals Hall.
      </p>

      <h3>Location of Desks</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Main terminal:</strong> Most rental desks are in the public arrivals area before security. Upon exiting baggage reclaim, desks are generally positioned to the right.</li>
        <li><strong>Car collection:</strong> After completing the paperwork at the desk, the rental car park is a short walk from the terminal building. No shuttle is required for agencies based within the terminal.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Agencies with On-Site Desks</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Avis / Budget</strong> — located before security, typically open from 07:00 to 23:00</li>
        <li><strong>Europcar</strong> — located before security, typically open from 07:00 to 00:00</li>
        <li><strong>Hertz</strong> — located before security, typically open from 07:00 to 00:00</li>
        <li><strong>Sixt</strong> — located before security, typically open from 06:00 to 00:00</li>
        <li><strong>Enterprise / National / Alamo</strong> — often share a service area or are serviced by the same provider (Guerin) within the terminal</li>
        <li><strong>Goldcar</strong> — located before security, typically open from 06:00 to 00:00</li>
        <li><strong>Guerin</strong> — Portuguese rental brand with a desk located before security</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Key Considerations</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Operating hours:</strong> Many desks operate until midnight, but late arrivals should still confirm exact pickup arrangements in advance.</li>
        <li><strong>Off-site agencies:</strong> Several low-cost or local agencies operate outside the terminal and do not have a desk in the main arrivals hall.</li>
        <li><strong>Documentation:</strong> You will usually need your reservation voucher, passport or ID, driver’s license, and a physical credit card for the security deposit. Exact requirements can vary by agency and vehicle class.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="off-airport-rental-providers">Off-Airport Rental Providers</h2>
      <p>
        Several popular providers operate just outside Faro Airport rather than directly inside the terminal. These
        off-airport agencies are a normal part of the Faro rental market and usually involve either a short shuttle
        ride or a short walk to a designated meeting point.
      </p>

      <h3>Off-Airport Agencies</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Airauto</strong> — operates out of Car Park 4 (P4), outside the main terminal desk area</li>
        <li><strong>Masterkings</strong> — well-regarded local provider located in a dedicated area at Car Park 4</li>
        <li><strong>Drive on Holidays</strong> — located on Rua Prof. Dr. Egas Moniz, close to the airport, with shuttle service</li>
        <li><strong>Green Motion</strong> — situated on Estrada Nacional 125, with shuttle pickup from the Kiss &amp; Fly area near Traveller’s Rest</li>
        <li><strong>Centauro</strong> — large regional operator with an off-site facility and shuttle transfer from outside arrivals</li>
        <li><strong>Record Go</strong> — located in the Montenegro area on Estrada do Aeroporto, with courtesy shuttle</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Where to Find the Shuttle or Meeting Point</h3>
      <p>
        If you book with an off-site provider, your confirmation voucher will usually direct you to one of two meeting areas:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Car Park 4 (P4):</strong> reached by following the Rent-a-Car signs through the pedestrian tunnel. This is the main hub for agencies such as Airauto and Masterkings.</li>
        <li><strong>Kiss &amp; Fly / Shuttle Zone:</strong> located directly outside the terminal and commonly used by off-terminal shuttle operators such as Centauro and Green Motion.</li>
      </ol>

      <h3>Why Travelers Choose Off-Airport</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Cost:</strong> Rates are often lower than at terminal-based counters.</li>
        <li><strong>Transparency:</strong> Some local providers are preferred by repeat visitors for simpler fuel or insurance policies.</li>
        <li><strong>Fleet variety:</strong> Larger off-site depots may offer more choice during peak season.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If you are traveling with children or a lot of luggage, it is worth checking whether the shuttle is a larger bus
        or a small van, since that can affect comfort and wait times in peak season.
      </p>

      <h2 id="how-pickup-usually-works">How Pickup Usually Works</h2>
      <p>
        The pickup process at Faro Airport is generally efficient, but it depends on whether your provider is inside
        the official airport rental setup or based off-site.
      </p>

      <h3>Step 1: Terminal Desk Check-In</h3>
      <p>
        Once you clear customs and enter the Arrivals Hall, head to your agency’s desk or meeting point.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Documentation:</strong> You will usually need a valid passport or ID, driver’s license, and a physical credit card in the main driver’s name for the deposit.</li>
        <li><strong>Rental agreement:</strong> You sign the contract and receive the key, along with a document showing the car’s condition and parking location.</li>
        <li><strong>Toll transponder:</strong> If needed, this is the point where you should ask about Via Verde or any toll device setup.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Step 2: The Walk to Car Park 4 (P4)</h3>
      <p>
        Nearly all on-site rentals at Faro use Car Park 4 (P4) as the primary collection point.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Location:</strong> Exit the terminal and follow the Rent-a-Car or P4 signs. The route is level and paved, with the car collection area a short walk from the terminal.</li>
        <li><strong>Meeting point:</strong> Some local or intermediate agencies do not maintain a desk in the terminal and instead use a meeting point or representative in the P4 area.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Step 3: Vehicle Inspection and Exit</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Locating the car:</strong> Your paperwork should list the exact bay number.</li>
        <li><strong>Damage check:</strong> Compare the car’s condition to the diagram provided and photograph anything not already noted before leaving.</li>
        <li><strong>Exiting:</strong> Use the key, ticket, or code provided to leave the parking barrier. Check the fuel gauge before you exit the airport grounds.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Summary of Pickup Locations</h3>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Agency Type</th>
            <th>Desk Location</th>
            <th>Vehicle Pickup Point</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
