            <td>Off-site depot</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h3>Pro-Tips</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Skip the line:</strong> Loyalty or fast-track programs may let you bypass the desk and go directly to a kiosk or bay.</li>
        <li><strong>Shuttle note:</strong> If your agency is off-site, double-check the pickup point on the voucher rather than assuming all airport rentals work the same way.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="leaving-the-airport-by-car">Leaving the Airport by Car</h2>
      <p>
        Leaving Faro Airport by car is relatively straightforward. The airport is served by a main access road that
        quickly connects to the Algarve’s primary routes.
      </p>

      <h3>1. Exiting the Rental Lot</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>The barrier:</strong> Most vehicles will open the parking gate automatically with the key, ticket, or validated access provided at pickup.</li>
        <li><strong>Initial direction:</strong> The exit leads onto the airport loop road and then toward the main roundabout.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>2. The Main Airport Roundabout</h3>
      <p>
        This is the first major navigation point after pickup.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Faro / N125:</strong> follow this for Faro city center or the national road that runs along the coast</li>
        <li><strong>A22 / Lisboa / Portimão / España:</strong> the main route for most tourists heading across the Algarve or toward the Spanish border</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>3. Getting onto the A22 (Via do Infante)</h3>
      <p>
        After leaving the roundabout, you continue along the N125-10 before joining the A22 interchange.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Heading west:</strong> follow signs for Portimão / Albufeira / Lisboa</li>
        <li><strong>Heading east:</strong> follow signs for Olhão / Tavira / España</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>4. Driving Conditions and Tips</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>A22:</strong> now that the motorway is toll-free, it is the easiest way to move across the Algarve quickly.</li>
        <li><strong>Speed limits:</strong> the airport roads are slower, while the A22 motorway is faster and more flowing.</li>
        <li><strong>N125 alternative:</strong> useful for shorter local trips, but noticeably slower and more stop-and-go than the motorway.</li>
        <li><strong>Fuel station:</strong> there is a BP station near the airport roundabout, which is useful when returning the car or stopping to reset your navigation.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>For First-Time Drivers</h3>
      <p>
        The first few kilometers feel like a warm-up. The real test is the first large roundabout and deciding whether
        you are heading into Faro, onto the N125, or directly onto the A22.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Roundabout etiquette:</strong> stay alert and use indicators clearly.</li>
        <li><strong>N125 vs A22:</strong> the A22 is usually the easier choice for first-time visitors leaving the airport.</li>
        <li><strong>Tailgating:</strong> local drivers may follow more closely than you are used to. Hold your line and move right when appropriate.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="when-renting-here-makes-sense">When Renting Here Makes Sense</h2>
      <p>
        Renting at Faro Airport is often one of the most practical choices in Portugal, but its value depends on the shape
        of the trip.
      </p>

      <h3>1. When the Itinerary Demands Flexibility</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Beach access:</strong> many of the Algarve’s most iconic coves and west-coast beaches are difficult to reach directly by public transport.</li>
        <li><strong>Regional exploration:</strong> Faro is a practical starting point for exploring inland Algarve towns and wider southern Portugal.</li>
        <li><strong>Road speed:</strong> the A22 makes airport pickup especially useful for travelers who want to move efficiently across the region.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>2. When Traveling as a Group or Family</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Cost efficiency:</strong> once you add multiple public transport tickets and the final taxi or rideshare leg, a rental can make more sense for families.</li>
        <li><strong>Luggage logistics:</strong> strollers, child seats, and multiple suitcases are much easier to manage with a car than with regional buses or trains.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>3. When Looking for the Best Value</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Inventory:</strong> airport fleets are usually larger than downtown fleets, which helps with choice and availability.</li>
        <li><strong>Avoiding small-town premiums:</strong> smaller pickup points can be more limited and may carry extra delivery or supply-related costs.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>When It Does Not Make Sense to Rent</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>One-town stays:</strong> if you are staying in a walkable center and only leaving once or twice, rideshare or occasional taxis may be simpler.</li>
        <li><strong>City-to-city travel:</strong> if your trip is only between Faro, Lisbon, and Porto, rail may be easier than dealing with city parking.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Quick Decision Guide</h3>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Rent at the Airport If...</th>
            <th>Skip the Rental If...</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>You are staying in a rural villa or apartment</td>
            <td>You are staying in a central hotel in Faro or Lagos</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>You want to visit multiple beaches</td>
            <td>You expect to spend most of your time in one place</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>You have children or bulky gear</td>
            <td>You are a solo traveler or light-packing couple</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>You want to explore inland Algarve or beyond</td>
            <td>You are mainly taking the train to Lisbon or Porto next</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
